@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+- **Projects with several folders.** Add extra folders to a project from its ⋯ menu in the sidebar (**Add a folder to this project…**; **Remove folder …** keeps the files). The agent reads, searches and edits in every project folder with the same approvals as the main folder, and the system prompt lists them; anything outside all of them still asks. Projects saved before load unchanged. A run still makes its worktree from the main folder's Git repository; in a run the extra folders are read-only (a write there asks every time and is not part of the changes you apply).
+
 ## 3.4.0 (2026-11-20)
 - **A desktop shell like the Antigravity App.**
   - A menu row (ORBIX, Workspace, View, Window) and a toolbar: the mark (a new conversation), the sidebar switch, **Back** and **Forward** (Alt+← / Alt+→) across conversations, Runs and Review, search, and where you are: project / conversation, with its state, running time and branch. In the Windows app the menu row is the title bar.
