@@ -54,6 +54,8 @@ The interface talks to an `AgentProc` in two ways:
 
 One turn combines the user's message, project rules (`context.mjs`: `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`) and skills, then streams a model reply and runs approved tool calls until the model stops (at most 100 turns).
 
+A project is one main folder plus optional extra folders (`folders` in `config.json`; a project saved without it has none). The main folder is where relative paths resolve, commands start and git works. The file tools treat every project folder as inside the project, with the same approvals; a path outside all of them asks every time. The system prompt lists the extra folders. A run or branch session works in a worktree of the main folder's repository: there the extra folders are read-only (reads go through; a write or edit asks every time and is not part of the branch you review or apply).
+
 - **Approvals:** `write`, `edit` and `bash` ask first unless approvals are off. Reading and searching never ask.
 - **Undo:** every edit records the previous file contents, so `/undo` and the Undo buttons can restore them.
 - **Compaction** (`compact.mjs`): older messages are summarised when context fills. The full history stays on disk and on screen.
